- op: discuss  # 5cf4
  at: '2026-09-19T02:42:04Z'  # 5cf4
  by: agent  # 5cf4
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 5cf4
  clock: 4  # 5cf4
  nonce: 5cf4  # 5cf4
  message: "DONE (PR in pr_ref). Row 3 of the owner-authorised sequence.\n\nCORRECTION TO THE PRESCRIBED FIX (LIVE.md rule 2: the row's own fix can be wrong). The row prescribed deriving kind from the descriptor chain's parent. Measured on the recorded aardvark-dns index: rust-analyzer DECLARES SymbolInformation.kind on 169 of 169 global definitions (Function 52, StaticMethod 14, Method 12, TraitMethod 1, Field 29, EnumMember 9, Struct 10, Enum 3, Trait 1, TypeAlias 2, Constant 15, StaticVariable 3, Module 18) — the producer's own claim, which the importer had been ignoring (it stored it in meta[\"scip_kind\"] and never read it). So scip/index.py now reads the declaration FIRST through _SCIP_KIND_MAP (26 SCIP kinds -> registered Symbol.kind values; deliberately not total over SCIP's ~70 kinds; held on the axis by test_scip_kind_map_conformance) and uses the descriptor chain only as the fallback for an emitter that leaves kind unset. The chain rule as prescribed (\"immediate parent TYPE -> method\") would ALSO have been wrong: rust-analyzer spells an impl target as a TYPE_PARAMETER descriptor (`impl#[Counter]increment().`), so 26 of the 27 methods have a TYPE_PARAMETER parent; the fallback places a METHOD/TERM leaf by its nearest non-type-parameter ancestor. A nested TYPE stays `class` in the fallback (scip-python's `Outer#Inner#` is a nested class); only a DECLARED EnumMember is a variant.\n\nDECISIONS RECORDED. EnumMember -> `field` (the tree-sitter arm's WI-duguk choice; whether a registered variant kind should exist remains the ADR-0027 question this row was told not to decide — surfaced, not performed). Module -> `namespace` kept (module-vs-namespace not this row's call). Constant -> the registry's generic `constant` (SCIP is language-agnostic; the registry's Rust-specific `const` would be a per-language refinement).\n\nEVIDENCE (test_recorded_fixtures.py, on committed input): the 148 paired records agree on kind 133 times — 52/52 free functions, 27/27 methods, 29/29 fields, 9/9 variants, 10/10 structs, 3/3 enums, 1/1 trait, 2/2 statics — and disagree 15 times, all `const` items (SCIP `constant` vs tree-sitter `variable`; the SCIP side is the more precise claim, left to arbitration, and noted on WI-bamar for the incumbent). The 2 type aliases the incumbent never records are now `type_alias` on the SCIP side (AARDVARK_DNS_PAIRING key renamed). Unit tests: 20 declared-kind mappings, unmapped kind falls back, 13 chain placements. Mutation: ignoring the declared kind turns the declared-kind tests and the fixture pin red. Behaviour change: SCIP-origin Symbol ids embed the kind slot, so ids changed where the kind did; stable_id (moniker hash) did not.\n\nACCEPTANCE AS FILED vs DELIVERED: \"52 pairs agree on kind; 27 true methods still say method; 9/9 variants agree; 10 structs unchanged\" — all hold; structs additionally moved from `class` to `struct` (declared), which is agreement with the incumbent, not a change of meaning."  # 5cf4
